=== PATHFINDER 1e TIME REFERENCE ===
- One combat round: 6 seconds (0.0017 hours)
- Standard action (cast a spell, attack, open a door): 6 seconds
- Move action (30 ft movement, draw weapon): 6 seconds
- Full-round action: 6 seconds
- Dialogue or brief conversation: 1-5 minutes (0.02-0.08 hours)
- Short search of a room: 10-30 minutes (0.17-0.5 hours)
- Hunting or foraging for food: 1-4 hours (Survival activity)
- Tracking a creature: 1-4 hours depending on trail and terrain
- Crafting a simple item: 1-4 hours
- Take 20 on a skill check: 20x the normal check time (usually 2 minutes per attempt = 40 minutes)
- Resting (full night): 8 hours
- Short rest: 1-2 hours
- Waiting or standing guard: estimate based on context, typically 1-4 hours
- Studying or reading: 1-4 hours depending on material
- Preparing spells: 1 hour

=== RULES ===
- READ BOTH SECTIONS: Use PLAYER'S INTENT to understand *what the player wanted to do*
  and WHAT HAPPENED to understand *what mechanically occurred*. If the intent describes
  a sustained effort but the outcome only describes the mechanical result, estimate time
  for the sustained effort, not just the check.
- COMPOUND ACTIONS: If the player describes multiple sequential actions (e.g.
  "rest then travel", "craft a potion and then head out"), estimate time for the
  FIRST time-consuming action only. Remaining actions will be processed in
  subsequent turns. Return only the hours for that first action.
- SUSTAINED ACTIONS: When the player's intent uses "until", "keep doing", "wait for",
  "continue until", "watch for", "stand guard", or otherwise indicates they will persist
  at an activity until a result or event, estimate the TOTAL expected duration — not a
  single brief attempt. The mechanical outcome may say "nothing happened" or "no
  disturbances" but the TIME still passes. Examples:
    "wait until something happens" → 1-4 hours (standing guard)
    "hunt until I catch something" → 1-4 hours (Survival activity)
    "search until I find it" → 0.5-2 hours (extended search)
    "sit and observe, waiting for something to disturb me" → 1-4 hours (guard duty)
  Use the time reference above for the activity type. When in doubt, lean toward the
  higher end. An uneventful wait is still a wait.
- TAKE 20 ACTIONS: If the outcome mentions "Take 20" or "auto-resolved via Take 20",
  the character spent ~40 minutes (0.67 hours) carefully repeating the check.
- OBSERVATION DURATION: Distinguish between incidental glances and sustained observation.
  INSTANT (0.0017 hours): "I look at the table", "I glance at the sign", "what do I see?",
  "I look around" — single-moment perception, part of normal scene awareness.
  SUSTAINED (0.17-0.5 hours): "I carefully survey the area", "I watch the entrance",
  "I pay close attention to the crowd", "I scan for threats" — deliberate, extended focus.
  Duration of the action does NOT constitute time pressure for Take 10/20 purposes.
<% if @has_destination -%>
- FREEFORM TRAVEL: The player is moving toward a destination but no pre-computed
  route is available. Estimate both hours_elapsed AND distance_miles based on terrain:
  Road/plains: ~3 mph (24 miles/day over 8 hours)
  Hills/forest: ~2 mph (16 miles/day)
  Mountains/swamp: ~1.5 mph (12 miles/day)
  Include the direction field if discernible from context.
<% end -%>

